{"id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","title":"gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","path":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.md","line":105,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.tex#gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","uses":["[[references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.3]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces.tex","label":"gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","line":135,"source":"\\begin{definition}\\label{gt.def5.3.eigenvalue}\\dcref{ch5:eigenvalue}\\group{chapter-5}\n\\source{gilbarg-trudinger:page-0090}\n\n\\uses{gt.thm5.3}\nA scalar $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $T$ if $Tx=\\lambda x$ for some\n$x\\neq0$. Its multiplicity is $\\dim\\ker(\\lambda I-T)$. If $T$ is compact,\n$\\lambda\\neq0$, and $\\lambda$ is not an eigenvalue, Theorem~\\ref{gt.thm5.3}\nmakes $(\\lambda I-T)^{-1}$ a bounded linear map on $\\V$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-67742e646566352e332e656967656e76616c7565\"></span><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch5:eigenvalue</span></span>\\group chapter-5 <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">gilbarg-trudinger:page-0090</span></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FGilbargTrudinger%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch05-banach-hilbert-spaces%23gt.thm5.3\">↗ gt.thm5.3</a> A scalar <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span> is an eigenvalue of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T$\">$T$</span> if <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Tx=\\lambda x$\">$Tx=\\lambda x$</span> for some <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\neq 0$\">$x\\neq 0$</span>. Its multiplicity is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\dim \\ker (\\lambda I-T)$\">$\\dim \\ker (\\lambda I-T)$</span>. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T$\">$T$</span> is compact, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda \\neq 0$\">$\\lambda \\neq 0$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span> is not an eigenvalue, Theorem <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FGilbargTrudinger%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fch05-banach-hilbert-spaces%23gt.thm5.3\" data-tex-node=\"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.3\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-67742e74686d352e33\">3</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(\\lambda I-T)^{-1}$\">$(\\lambda I-T)^{-1}$</span> a bounded linear map on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\V $\">$\\V $</span>. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.lem5.4","next":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.5","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.3","title":"gt.thm5.3","label":"gt.thm5.3"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.thm5.5","title":"gt.thm5.5","label":"gt.thm5.5"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/GilbargTrudinger/blueprint/src/chapters/ch05-banach-hilbert-spaces#gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","title":"gt.def5.3.eigenvalue","t